00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.990 align:start position:0%
eu transport ministers have agreed on a  proposal assigning new tasks to the  european railway agency and streamlining  its processes  the agency would act as a one-stop shop  for authorizing vehicles for  cross-border operations and for issuing  safety certificates to railway  undertakings across member states  the proposed regulation is part of the  fourth railway package published by the  european commission  this constitutes a first step  we need to move on to  next steps  in the near future  so that we can try to complete a common  european policy for rail transport in  europe that's going to have a big impact  on the economy  and on development in the eu  ministers have also adopted their  position on a proposal to develop a  coordinated eu approach to research and  innovation in the rail sector  the idea is to set up a public private  partnership shift to rail to support the  development of better rail services in  europe and boost the rail sector's  competitiveness  in other developments the council also  held a policy debate on competitive and  resource efficient urban mobility
 

